  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Read each lane as one IFTTT recipe",
      "items": [
        "Col 0 is the IF (the reading crosses a band), col 1 is an AND IF (a refinement applies), col 2 is the THEN (a finished phrase)",
        "The thresholds live at the top of each domain's own module, in the same units its phrase uses - nothing is hand-waved into a magic word"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Real numbers, tuned by feel",
      "items": [
        "SUN_BAND_STRONG_WM2 was tuned down from 600 to 450 W/m2: a clear 500 W/m2 sky already reads as genuinely intense in practice, not merely \"sunny\"",
        "The 45deg direction-shift and 10mph gust-excess rules exist so a few degrees of wander or an ordinary gust can't manufacture a signal out of noise - rain's trend rule follows the same idea"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Clothing triggers off bands, not raw numbers",
      "items": [
        "clothing.ts never reads mph or mm directly - it triggers off the same TempBand the feels sentence already names, plus a rain/dry flag, so \"it feels mild\" and \"wear a jumper\" can never disagree",
        "Wind was dropped from the clothing rule entirely (2026-09-01): the real wardrobe has no wind-specific item, so there is nothing for a wind reading to trigger"
      ]
    }
  ]
